cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  PET depolymerisation database: extracted experiments, LLM judge audit, and the
  code that built them
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite the paper below. The dataset in
  data/ is CC BY 4.0, which asks for attribution; this is it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: bin Javaid
    given-names: Muhammad
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
  - family-names: Ben Hicham
    given-names: Karim K.
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
  - family-names: Battulga
    given-names: Enkhnyam
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
  - family-names: Mitsos
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
  - family-names: Grohe
    given-names: Martin
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
repository-code: https://github.com/Enkhnyam/pet-depolymerisation-database
abstract: >-
  3,942 homogeneous catalytic poly(ethylene terephthalate) depolymerisation
  experiments extracted from 561 full-text articles by a schema-enforced LLM
  extractor and audited record-by-record against those articles by an
  independent LLM judge. Each record carries the chunk identifiers its values
  were read from, the judge's verdict and critique, and the values the judge
  would have substituted. Also included: the 295-experiment hand-curated
  reference key used to validate the judge, and the extraction and evaluation
  code.
keywords:
  - PET depolymerisation
  - chemical recycling
  - homogeneous catalysis
  - information extraction
  - large language models
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - research data
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/Enkhnyam/pet-depolymerisation-database/blob/main/NOTICE.md
